" ------------------------ SUMMARY of DISTRIBUTION -------------------------------"



# | Group             | Includes                                                             | Relationship                    |
# | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
# | **Discrete**      | Poisson, Zipf                                                        | Count things                    |
# | **Continuous**    | Normal, Logistic, Uniform, Exponential, Pareto, Rayleigh, Chi-square | Measure values or time          |
# | **Power law**     | Pareto, Zipf                                                         | Few big things, many small ones |
# | **Time-based**    | Poisson (how often), Exponential (how long between)                  | Related                         |
# | **Visualization** | Seaborn                                                              | Used to see shape of all above  |

"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~"

# | Term                  | Simple Meaning                              |
# | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
# | Random Numbers        | Any unpredictable number                    |
# | Data Distributions    | Random numbers following a shape/pattern    |
# | Permutation/Shuffling | Mixing the order of data randomly           |
# | Seaborn               | Tool to plot and see data visually          |
# | Normal (Gaussian)     | Bell-shaped curve (average is common)       |
# | Poisson               | How many times something happens            |
# | Uniform               | All values equally likely                   |
# | Logistic              | Like normal, but steeper                    |
# | Exponential           | Time between events                         |
# | Chi-square            | For stats and testing                       |
# | Rayleigh              | Signal-related modeling                     |
# | Pareto                | 80/20 rule - few big, many small            |
# | Zipf                  | Few items happen a lot (e.g., common words) |

"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~"

# | **Distribution** | **Shape When `a=2`**            | **Shape When `a=60`**          | **Use Case**                           | **Example**              |
# | ---------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |
# | **Normal**       | Wide bell curve                 | Narrow bell curve              | Natural phenomena, test scores         | Height of students       |
# | **Poisson**      | Spread counts (more variance)   | Sharp spike at 60              | Count of events over time              | Emails per hour          |
# | **Uniform**      | Equal chance across [0,2]       | Equal chance across [0,60]     | Random picks, simulations              | Dice roll                |
# | **Logistic**     | Bell-like but steeper sides     | Very steep and narrow bell     | Used in ML classification              | Logistic regression      |
# | **Exponential**  | Long tail, more spread          | Very short tail, tight values  | Time between events                    | Time between buses       |
# | **Chi-square**   | Asymmetric, positive values     | Very sharp peak, small spread  | Hypothesis testing, stats              | Chi-square test          |
# | **Rayleigh**     | Peak shifted right, smooth tail | Peak closer to 0, sharp drop   | Signal processing, wind speed modeling | Wireless signal strength |
# | **Pareto**       | Heavy long tail (many big vals) | Spiky near 1, few large values | 80/20 rule modeling                    | Income distribution      |
# | **Zipf**         | Long tail (many high numbers)   | Mostly 1s, few large values    | Word frequency, NLP                    | "the" vs rare words      |
